WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.490
- Apple just gave its iPhone 14 models

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.110
a new Satellite connection.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.180
Ah, okay. We're connected.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.400
If you need help, it can
be used to send a message

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.870
to emergency services,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.630
when you don't have cellular
or Wi-Fi connectivity.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.120
To test this, I'm not exactly off grid.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.920
I'm in Prospect Park in Brooklyn,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.540
and Apple gave me this test phone,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.460
where the cellular radio is disabled

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.830
so the Satellite connectivity kicks in.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.652
The only thing I needed next,

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:25.650
(dummy squeaks)

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.523
an emergency.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.430
While that creates a pretty staged demo,

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.610
where little can go wrong, I
still got a really good sense

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.320
of how this feature works

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.080
and how extremely limited
the feature is compared

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.210
to other satellite devices.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.940
Okay, yes let's say fake Joanna falls.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.943
Ready? Bye.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:50.010
So I call 911, but
there's no cell service.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.380
So instead the iPhone shows this.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.900
An emergency text via satellite button.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.880
When I select that, I get this screen

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.130
where I can select from these options.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.560
There are some additional
things to answer too.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.610
Who needs help? Me, always.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.340
Chest pain, traumatic injury, sickness,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.023
stroke, drowning, other.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.900
Traumatic injury.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.650
I can also decide if I wanna
alert my emergency contact.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.260
Now comes the connection
to the satellites,

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.760
which in the demos took anywhere

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.340
from a few seconds to a minute.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.290
It's looking for a signal.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:26.990
Okay, I'm gonna turn to the right.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.460
The phone prompts you to move

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.720
in different directions

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.060
to be better in line with the Satellite,

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.270
which if I really did fall,
would be a bit of an issue.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.312
To the right, to the
right like Beyonce says.

00:01:39.312 --> 00:01:42.780
(upbeat music)

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.280
As soon as it connects, a message

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.080
with the information you just filled out

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.630
begins to be sent via Satellite.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.190
But here's the interesting thing.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.290
Those messages may not go directly

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.570
to emergency services yet.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.810
If your local responders
don't accept text messages,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.281
the message goes to an Apple Relay Center,

00:02:00.281 --> 00:02:02.880
where a person will then
relay the information

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.166
to local responders to
get you the help you need.

00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:08.520
In either case, a dispatcher may ask

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.980
for some additional questions via text.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.680
Describe the location of the emergency.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.680
Near a bridge and a path and a tree.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.570
It takes much longer for
the messages to go through

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.280
than when on a cellular connection.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.830
So Apple suggests keeping
the messages shorter,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.603
so there's less data to send.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.580
Okay the local responders
have been notified of my fall.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.520
In the case of this demo, Apple
has cut off those messages

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.830
from actual emergency workers.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.720
Like any piece of Satellite equipment,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.720
the phone has to be outside
with a clear view of the sky,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.270
so it can connect to a satellite.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.750
Apparently this extra,
I don't know, two feet

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:52.860
doesn't help at all.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.197
In one test, I did run
into a connection issue.

00:02:56.197 --> 00:02:58.200
"Uh-oh turn right to find the satellite."

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.760
I'm not connected anymore.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.700
It's also more limited than
a dedicated satellite device,

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.700
like the $400 Garmin inReach
Mini 2 and the $250 Spot-X.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.220
Those devices let you
contact emergency services,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.070
but also message friends or family.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.710
I miss typing on these so much.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.760
With the iPhone feature,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.790
your emergency contact will be
able to see your conversation

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.690
with the emergency dispatcher,
but they can't respond.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.190
The Garmin and Spot-X,

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.860
however do require monthly subscriptions.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.760
Apple says this feature is
free for the first two years.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.560
My guess is that Apple's
keeping this feature free

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.740
for now because, well,
who would pay for it?

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:40.320
Maybe I would, if I was
frequently in places

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.630
without reliable cellular service.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.210
But even then I may opt
for one of these devices

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.940
that actually lets me
text family or friends.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.860
I wouldn't be surprised
to see Apple build its

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.870
satellite features up over time,

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.840
and perhaps make some available for a fee.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.240
For now, like the car
crash detection feature,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.470
this is a cool piece of mind
perk for iPhone 14 owners.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.870
I just wouldn't fall for it.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:07.863
Smile. You really took
a fall for the team.

